      "observed": "J11 is a Screw_Terminal_01x02 with pin 2 connected to the GPIO1/heater control net (/Microcontroller/NET0016), which also connects to U2 pin 13 (GPIO1), U4 pins 1 and 2 (IN, DIAG_EN), and D1 pin 2.",
      "expected": "The specification describes J11 as a Barrel_Jack for the 12 V run supply, and does not mention any screw terminal on the heater control input. The heater control net should only connect to the MCU GPIO1 and the high-side switch inputs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"J11\") (value \"Screw_Terminal_01x02\") (footprint \"TerminalBlock_4Ucon:TerminalBlock_4Ucon_1x02_P3.50mm_Horizontal\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"6\") (name \"/Microcontroller/NET0016\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D1\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J11\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"GPIO1/ADC1_CH1/XTAL_32K_N\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"IN\") (pintype \"input\")) (node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"DIAG_EN\") (pintype \"input\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "J11 (Barrel_Jack) → +12V net."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Exposes the MCU GPIO1 and the TPS1H200 input to external wiring via a screw terminal, allowing external override of the heater control signal or potential damage from miswiring.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an extra screw terminal (J11) connected directly to the ESP32 GPIO1 and the TPS1H200 heater switch input, which is not present in the specification and could allow external control or damage to the heater control signal."
}

